@startuml sequence-centralized-voter
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #01579B
    ActorBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ParticipantBorderColor #01579B
}

participant "Node A" as nodeA
participant "Node B" as nodeB
participant "Node C" as nodeC
participant "Voter\n(Central)" as voter
participant "Output" as output

autonumber

note over nodeA, voter
  Centralized Voter Topology
  Dedicated voting CPU/processor
end note

nodeA ->> nodeA: process()
nodeB ->> nodeB: process()
nodeC ->> nodeC: process()

nodeA ->> voter: send_result(A=GREEN)
note right of nodeA: Node A sends its result

nodeB ->> voter: send_result(B=GREEN)
note right of nodeB: Node B sends its result

nodeC ->> voter: send_result(C=RED)
note right of nodeC: Node C sends its result (disagrees)

voter ->> voter: receive_all()
note right of voter: Voter collects all results

voter ->> voter: count_votes()
note right of voter: Count: GREEN=2, RED=1

voter ->> voter: voting_2oo3()
note right of voter: Majority vote: GREEN wins

voter ->> voter: identify_fault()
note right of voter: Node C disagrees\nNode C is faulty

par Broadcast Decision
    voter ->> nodeA: decision(GREEN)
    voter ->> nodeB: decision(GREEN)
    voter ->> nodeC: decision(GREEN)
    note right of voter: All nodes learn decision
end

nodeA ->> output: send(GREEN)
note right of nodeA: A executes decision

nodeB ->> output: send(GREEN)
note right of nodeB: B executes decision

nodeC ->> output: log_fault()
note right of nodeC: C logged as faulty\n(optional execute)

output ->> output: execute()

note over nodeA, output
  Centralized Voter Advantages:
  ✓ Separates voting from processing
  ✓ Simpler application logic
  ✓ Centralized policy/configuration
  ✓ Easy to debug voting logic

  Centralized Voter Disadvantages:
  ✗ Voter becomes single point of failure
  ✗ Network latency critical
  ✗ Voter node must be certified
  ✗ Scalability limited by voter throughput
end note

@enduml
